# {{ customer }} — {{ solution }} Knowledge Model

## Purpose

Define the concepts, relationships, statuses, identifiers, and modelling rules used by this blueprint.

## Conceptual Model

```text
Consumer → participates in → Business Use Case
Consumer → consumes → Data Product
Business Use Case → requires → Required Capability
Source → feeds → Data Flow
Data Flow → produces or updates → Data Product
Quality Control → assures → Data Flow or Data Product
Operational Capability → operates or supports → Data Flow or Data Product
Technology → realizes or constrains → implementation
ADR → shapes → architecture records
```

## Concepts

| Concept | Identifier | Definition |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Consumer | CON-NNN | Person, team, organisation, public audience, or system that uses information or participates in an outcome. |
| Source | SRC-NNN | Real external system or provider that originates or externally curates data. |
| Technology | TECH-NNN | Named product, service, platform, engine, or material implementation pattern. |
| Business Use Case | UC-NNN | Distinct consumer outcome, decision, accountability, or obligation supported by data. |
| Required Capability | RC-NNN | Implementation-independent statement of required functional and non-functional ability. |
| Data Product | DP-NNN | Managed information offering for defined consumers and purposes. |
| Data Flow | DF-NNN | Logical movement and transformation path from source or product to target product or destination. |
| Quality Control | QC-NNN | Preventive, detective, or corrective trust mechanism. |
| Operational Capability | OC-NNN | Repeatable ability to run, observe, recover, secure, scale, deploy, or retire the solution. |
| Architecture Decision Record | ADR-NNN | Record of a material architecture choice, rationale status, alternatives, and consequences. |

